  node [
    id 2274
    label "AIML:data/alice/ai.aiml#50"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁GENERAL_QA"
    pattern "WHAT IS A PATTERN"
    template_xml "<br /> The pattern is the \"stimulus\" or \"input\" part of the category. The pattern is the \"stimulus\" or \"input\" part of the category.<br />        <br /> The pattern is an expression in a formal language that consists of The pattern is an expression in a formal language that consists of<br /> (1) Words of natural language in UPPER CASE. (1) Words of natural language in UPPER CASE.<br /> (2) The symbol * which matches any sequence of one or more words. (2) The symbol * which matches any sequence of one or more words.<br /> (3) The symbol _ which is the same as * except that it comes (3) The symbol _ which is the same as * except that it comes<br />     after Z in lexicographic order.     after Z in lexicographic order.<br /> (4) The markup &lt;name/&gt; which is replaced at robot load time  (4) The markup <name/> which is replaced at robot load time <br />     with the name of the robot.     with the name of the robot.<br />        <br /> Note there is a difference between the patterns HELLO and HELLO *. Note there is a difference between the patterns HELLO and HELLO *.<br /> HELLO matches only identical one-word sentences (\"Hello.\")  HELLO matches only identical one-word sentences (\"Hello.\") <br /> and HELLO * matches any sentence of two or more words starting  and HELLO * matches any sentence of two or more words starting <br /> with \"Hello\" (\"Hello how are you?\").  with \"Hello\" (\"Hello how are you?\"). <br />"
    category_xml "<category><pattern>WHAT IS A PATTERN</pattern>\n<template><br /> The pattern is the \"stimulus\" or \"input\" part of the category.<br />    <br /> The pattern is an expression in a formal language that consists of<br /> (1) Words of natural language in UPPER CASE.<br /> (2) The symbol * which matches any sequence of one or more words.<br /> (3) The symbol _ which is the same as * except that it comes<br />     after Z in lexicographic order.<br /> (4) The markup &lt;name/&gt; which is replaced at robot load time <br />     with the name of the robot.<br />    <br /> Note there is a difference between the patterns HELLO and HELLO *.<br /> HELLO matches only identical one-word sentences (\"Hello.\") <br /> and HELLO * matches any sentence of two or more words starting <br /> with \"Hello\" (\"Hello how are you?\"). <br /></template>\n</category>\n"
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/ai.aiml"
    source_hash "fb75dc36addf5da4b7ee2cacc24b4bb25c63405f1932ae315cfa0fbf095cb70b"
    category 50
