  node [
    id 2301
    label "AIML:data/alice/ai.aiml#77"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁GENERAL_QA"
    pattern "WHAT IS XML"
    template_xml "<br /> David Bacon pronounces it \"Eggsmell\".  XML is the Extensible David Bacon pronounces it \"Eggsmell\".  XML is the Extensible<br /> Markup Language.  Like many \"standards\" in computer science, XML Markup Language.  Like many \"standards\" in computer science, XML<br /> is a moving target.  In the simplest terms, XML is just a generalized is a moving target.  In the simplest terms, XML is just a generalized<br /> version of HTML.  Anyone is free to define new XML tags, which version of HTML.  Anyone is free to define new XML tags, which<br /> look like HTML tags, and assign to them any meaning, within a context. look like HTML tags, and assign to them any meaning, within a context.<br /> AIML is an example of using the XML standard to define a specialized AIML is an example of using the XML standard to define a specialized<br /> language for artificial intelligence.   language for artificial intelligence.  <br />        <br /> One reason to use an XML language is that there are numerous tools One reason to use an XML language is that there are numerous tools<br /> to edit and manipulate XML format files.  Another reason is that an to edit and manipulate XML format files.  Another reason is that an<br /> XML language is easy for people to learn, if they are already XML language is easy for people to learn, if they are already<br /> familiar with HTML.  Third, AIML programs contain a mixture of familiar with HTML.  Third, AIML programs contain a mixture of<br /> AIML and HTML (and in principle other XML languages), a considerable  AIML and HTML (and in principle other XML languages), a considerable <br /> convenience for programming web chat robots. convenience for programming web chat robots.<br />        <br /> A good resource for information on XML is www.oasis-open.org. A good resource for information on XML is www.oasis-open.org.<br />        <br />"
    category_xml "<category><pattern>WHAT IS XML</pattern>\n<template><br /> David Bacon pronounces it \"Eggsmell\".  XML is the Extensible<br /> Markup Language.  Like many \"standards\" in computer science, XML<br /> is a moving target.  In the simplest terms, XML is just a generalized<br /> version of HTML.  Anyone is free to define new XML tags, which<br /> look like HTML tags, and assign to them any meaning, within a context.<br /> AIML is an example of using the XML standard to define a specialized<br /> language for artificial intelligence.  <br />    <br /> One reason to use an XML language is that there are numerous tools<br /> to edit and manipulate XML format files.  Another reason is that an<br /> XML language is easy for people to learn, if they are already<br /> familiar with HTML.  Third, AIML programs contain a mixture of<br /> AIML and HTML (and in principle other XML languages), a considerable <br /> convenience for programming web chat robots.<br />    <br /> A good resource for information on XML is www.oasis-open.org.<br />    <br /></template>\n</category>\n"
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/ai.aiml"
