  node [
    id 2530
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#43"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN FOLD LATTICE AND THE INCIDENCE MATRIX"
    template_xml "The fold lattice is the algebraic structure induced by B (fold-phase incidence matrix). B*B^T gives fold-to-fold overlap; B^T*B gives phase-to-phase reachability via shared folds. The weighted version B*W_E*B^T is the topological score surface used in semantic_fold."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN FOLD LATTICE AND THE INCIDENCE MATRIX</pattern>\n    <template>The fold lattice is the algebraic structure induced by B (fold-phase incidence matrix). B*B^T gives fold-to-fold overlap; B^T*B gives phase-to-phase reachability via shared folds. The weighted version B*W_E*B^T is the topological score surface used in semantic_fold.</template>\n  </category>\n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
