  node [
    id 2552
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#65"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "WHAT IS A PERCEPTION FIELD IN KHANARY"
    template_xml "F_Q is an ephemeral 256-dimensional vector created at Pop phase by embed(query, confidence_context). It encodes the query direction in field space via sin-hash projection weighted 70% query / 30% context. It is L1-normalized and reset at Xul."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>WHAT IS A PERCEPTION FIELD IN KHANARY</pattern>\n    <template>F_Q is an ephemeral 256-dimensional vector created at Pop phase by embed(query, confidence_context). It encodes the query direction in field space via sin-hash projection weighted 70% query / 30% context. It is L1-normalized and reset at Xul.</template>\n  </category>\n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 65
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2545
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2552
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2553
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#66"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "HOW DOES F Q EMBED A QUERY INTO A FIELD VECTOR"
    template_xml "embed() hashes the canonicalized query string, then for each dimension i computes sin((hash_byte * 0.1) + i) blended with the confidence_context[i]. The result is L1-normalized so the field lies on the probability simplex, making cosine comparisons stable."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>HOW DOES F Q EMBED A QUERY INTO A FIELD VECTOR</pattern>\n    <template>embed() hashes the canonicalized query string, then for each dimension i computes sin((hash_byte * 0.1) + i) blended with the confidence_context[i]. The result is L1-normalized so the field lies on the probability simplex, making cosine comparisons stable.</template>\n  </category>\n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 66
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2546
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2553
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2554
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#67"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "WHAT IS COSINE SIMILARITY IN THE CONTEXT OF SEMANTIC FIELDS"
    template_xml "R_µ(Q) = clamp01((dot(F_Q, K_µ) / (|F_Q|·|K_µ|) + 1) / 2) where K_µ is the 256D sin-hash projection of the micronaut id. It measures directional alignment: 1.0 means perfect alignment, 0.5 is orthogonal, 0.0 is anti-aligned."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>WHAT IS COSINE SIMILARITY IN THE CONTEXT OF SEMANTIC FIELDS</pattern>\n    <template>R_µ(Q) = clamp01((dot(F_Q, K_µ) / (|F_Q|·|K_µ|) + 1) / 2) where K_µ is the 256D sin-hash projection of the micronaut id. It measures directional alignment: 1.0 means perfect alignment, 0.5 is orthogonal, 0.0 is anti-aligned.</template>\n  </category>\n\n  \n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 67
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2547
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2554
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2555
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#68"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "HOW DOES A 3D FIELD VECTOR RELATE TO A 256 DIMENSIONAL PERCEPTION FIELD"
    template_xml "The 3D refined_field_vec from a WCR delta is a directional hint from Gemma's question session. apply_wcr_delta() projects it to 256D via rx*sin(i*1.1)+ry*cos(i*0.9)+rz*sin(i*1.3+0.5), then blends into F_Q with alpha=delta_r. The 3D vector encodes semantic direction; the 256D field encodes query context."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>HOW DOES A 3D FIELD VECTOR RELATE TO A 256 DIMENSIONAL PERCEPTION FIELD</pattern>\n    <template>The 3D refined_field_vec from a WCR delta is a directional hint from Gemma's question session. apply_wcr_delta() projects it to 256D via rx*sin(i*1.1)+ry*cos(i*0.9)+rz*sin(i*1.3+0.5), then blends into F_Q with alpha=delta_r. The 3D vector encodes semantic direction; the 256D field encodes query context.</template>\n  </category>\n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 68
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2548
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2555
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2556
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#69"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN THE WCR SCORE AND THE SEMANTIC FIELD"
    template_xml "S_µ(Q) = W_µ · C_µ · R_µ(Q). W comes from the semantic graph arc weights; C from ConfidenceStore; R from the cosine of F_Q against µ's hash projection. The field F_Q directly determines R, so shifting F_Q via ΔR nudges the ranking of all micronauts simultaneously."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>WHAT IS THE RELATION BETWEEN THE WCR SCORE AND THE SEMANTIC FIELD</pattern>\n    <template>S_µ(Q) = W_µ · C_µ · R_µ(Q). W comes from the semantic graph arc weights; C from ConfidenceStore; R from the cosine of F_Q against µ's hash projection. The field F_Q directly determines R, so shifting F_Q via ΔR nudges the ranking of all micronauts simultaneously.</template>\n  </category>\n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 69
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2549
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2556
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2557
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#70"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "HOW DOES DELTA R REFINE THE PERCEPTION FIELD TOWARD A MICRONAUT"
    template_xml "apply_wcr_delta() blends a target vector T into F_Q: F_Q[i] = (1-alpha)*F_Q[i] + alpha*T[i], then L1-renormalizes. T is derived from refined_field_vec (Gemma's 3D hint) or falls back to the micronaut id hash. The blend alpha is capped at 0.15 per session."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>HOW DOES DELTA R REFINE THE PERCEPTION FIELD TOWARD A MICRONAUT</pattern>\n    <template>apply_wcr_delta() blends a target vector T into F_Q: F_Q[i] = (1-alpha)*F_Q[i] + alpha*T[i], then L1-renormalizes. T is derived from refined_field_vec (Gemma's 3D hint) or falls back to the micronaut id hash. The blend alpha is capped at 0.15 per session.</template>\n  </category>\n\n  \n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 70
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2550
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2557
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2558
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#71"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "IS THE L1 NORMALIZED FIELD A VALID PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION PROXY"
    template_xml "Yes with caveats. L1 normalization ensures the field sums to 1 over its absolute values, which is necessary for a probability distribution over dimensions. However, the field contains negative values from sin projections, so it is a signed measure rather than a true probability distribution. The cosine similarity computation treats it as a direction vector regardless."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>IS THE L1 NORMALIZED FIELD A VALID PROBABILITY DISTRIBUTION PROXY</pattern>\n    <template>Yes with caveats. L1 normalization ensures the field sums to 1 over its absolute values, which is necessary for a probability distribution over dimensions. However, the field contains negative values from sin projections, so it is a signed measure rather than a true probability distribution. The cosine similarity computation treats it as a direction vector regardless.</template>\n  </category>\n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
    category 71
    wildcard_count 0
    projection_order 2551
    default_bias 1.0
    authority "candidate_only"
  ]
  edge [
    source 4
    target 2558
    relation "contains_aiml_category"
    status "source_projection"
  ]
  node [
    id 2559
    label "AIML:data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml#72"
    kind "aiml_category"
    field "⟁KNOWLEDGE"
    pattern "DOES BLENDING REFINED FIELD VEC IMPROVE COSINE SIMILARITY WITH THE TARGET MICRONAUT"
    template_xml "Yes, when refined_field_vec is derived from Gemma's question answer about the micronaut. The blend moves F_Q toward the 256D direction of the micronaut id hash, increasing dot product and therefore R_µ(Q). The cap at alpha=0.15 prevents any single session from fully capturing the field."
    category_xml "<category>\n    <pattern>DOES BLENDING REFINED FIELD VEC IMPROVE COSINE SIMILARITY WITH THE TARGET MICRONAUT</pattern>\n    <template>Yes, when refined_field_vec is derived from Gemma's question answer about the micronaut. The blend moves F_Q toward the 256D direction of the micronaut id hash, increasing dot product and therefore R_µ(Q). The cap at alpha=0.15 prevents any single session from fully capturing the field.</template>\n  </category>\n\n  \n  "
    template_kind "response"
    source "data/alice/graph-fold-field.aiml"
    source_hash "690b763c21b759fec7c66a63139956587e8ab3aa63a2ceaf6c8dff9093fcca78"
